---
source: tests/help_snapshots.rs
---
Show the usage hours of recent runs, newest first.

Columns: RUN ID, STARTED, ENDED, HOURS. STARTED and ENDED are the start and end
of the billable usage of the run. HOURS is rounded to the minute, as `Xh Ym`.

With --rollup, each row is the total of one day, week, or month. A run counts in
the period in which it ended. A week starts on Monday. Columns: DATE, RUNS,
HOURS. DATE is the last day of the period. The rows are the --limit periods that
end with the current period, and a period with no runs shows 0.

Times and periods are in the local timezone. Add --utc to show them in UTC.

--after and --before select runs by the time that they ended: --after includes a
run that ended at that time, and --before does not. Each takes a date, which is
the start of that day, or an RFC 3339 time. With --rollup, a period is in the
output when it holds a selected time. When a filter cuts a period, the total of
that period includes only the runs inside the filter.

--limit counts rows: runs, or periods with --rollup. The default is 10. The
filters select which rows the limit keeps:
  no filter or --before    the newest rows (before --before)
  --after                  the oldest rows from --after
  --after and --before     every row between them; --limit is not allowed
The rows always show newest first.

Examples:
  snouty runs usage
  snouty runs usage --rollup week -n 4
  snouty runs usage --rollup month --after 2026-01-01
  snouty runs usage --after 2026-10-01 --before 2026-11-01 --utc

Add --json for machine-readable output. Each row prints as one JSON object on
its own line. A run has the fields run_id, hours, start_time, and end_time; the
times are RFC 3339 with the offset of the timezone. A period has the fields
date, runs, and hours, with hours rounded to hundredths:
  snouty --json runs usage --rollup month | jq -r '"\(.date) \(.hours)"'

Usage: snouty runs usage [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --rollup <ROLLUP>
          Total the runs of each day, week, or month
          
          [possible values: day, week, month]

      --after <AFTER>
          Only show runs that ended at or after this date (e.g. 2026-10-01) or
          RFC 3339 time

      --before <BEFORE>
          Only show runs that ended before this date (e.g. 2026-11-01) or RFC
          3339 time

      --utc
          Show times and periods in UTC instead of the local timezone

  -n, --limit <LIMIT>
          Maximum number of rows to display: runs, or periods with --rollup
          [default: 10; not allowed with both --after and --before]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

      --json
          Output JSON where supported (NDJSON for list/stream commands, pretty
          JSON otherwise)

      --verbose
          Log API requests to stderr (authentication tokens redacted)

      --settings <SETTINGS>
          Path to the snouty settings file (default: ./.snouty.toml; overrides
          SNOUTY_SETTINGS_PATH)

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Settings profile to select (overrides ANTITHESIS_PROFILE)
